WEBVTT


00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:06.330
You are not limited to using DesignaKnit
or the PC 10 controller for stitch

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:09.480
patterns on electronics
Silver Reed knitting machines.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:15.180
Combined Cochenile Stitch Painter and
the Silver Knit pattern controller for a

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.610
powerful, easy to use alternative.

00:00:19.515 --> 00:00:23.595
If you want to follow along, make sure
that you're familiar with the basics of

00:00:23.595 --> 00:00:24.405
Stitch Painter.

00:00:25.215 --> 00:00:30.135
Follow the instructions for installing the
Silver Knitt utility software and connect

00:00:30.135 --> 00:00:31.305
all the cables.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:37.005
Let's explore this powerful combination
of tools that will change how you use your

00:00:37.005 --> 00:00:37.605
knitting machine.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:44.350
Click the shortcut to
the Silver Knit utility.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.650
A simple interface is displayed.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.580
It opens with the last
file that you worked with.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:54.550
Let's open a new Ptitch Painter file.

00:00:55.450 --> 00:01:01.620
Click browse and select
your file ending with STC.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.740
The first thing you'll notice is a
preview of the stitch you selected.

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:11.270
The number of stitches and rows are
indicated as well as the knitting method.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:14.780
We'll talk about the knitting
method in another tutorial.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:22.190
Click the preview button for a larger
image and you can examine exactly what

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:26.930
information will download to the Silver
Knit controller and then to your knitting

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:27.410
machine.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.970
At the top is shown the stitch pattern
that you just selected at the bottom is

00:01:38.970 --> 00:01:42.480
shown the stitch pattern that
currently resides in the controller.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.200
Now you'll click download to transfer the
design created in Stitch Painter that you

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.440
just uploaded to the
Silver KNit controller.

00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:59.100
Before the download starts, you have
a number of options for modifying and

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.840
personalizing the stitch pattern.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:03.390
We'll discuss these later.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.940
For now, accept the defaults,
select your machine and click OK.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:14.850
You'll see a progress bar as the
pattern is downloaded to the controller.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:19.380
When the download is complete,
you'll see your pattern name shown.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.980
Click knit to start knitting.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:33.079
Here is the Silver Knit
interactive kitting screen.

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:38.200
Your entire pattern is shown in color
with row number indicators on the left.

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:43.269
As you move your carriage back and forth,
your patterning needles are selected.

00:02:43.899 --> 00:02:46.630
Notice the directional
indicators on each side.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:05.420
Now if you need to go back or rip a
few rows, you can do it here on screen.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:08.060
Just click the row where
you'd like to start knitting.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:16.340
Other tutorials about using Stitch Painter
and the Silver Knit pattern controller are

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.070
available in the Knit
it Now learning library.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:24.320
Please consider purchasing Stitch Painter
and the Silver Knit pattern controller by

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.400
clicking the links.

